{"PageNumber":8,"Angle":0,"RotatedAngle":0,"Height":2526,"Width":1786,"OriginHeight":0,"OriginWidth":0,"Elements":[{"Index":0,"Type":"Discard_type","Text":"TLI493D-A2B6","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":122},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":76},"RightBottom":{"X":404,"Y":122},"RightTop":{"X":404,"Y":76}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":1,"Type":"header","Text":"infineon","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":1369,"Y":175},"LeftTop":{"X":1369,"Y":54},"RightBottom":{"X":1667,"Y":175},"RightTop":{"X":1667,"Y":54}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":2,"Type":"title","Text":"#  Specification","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":233},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":192},"RightBottom":{"X":340,"Y":233},"RightTop":{"X":340,"Y":192}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":3,"Type":"title","Text":"##  3.2 Operating Range","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":339},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":291},"RightBottom":{"X":599,"Y":339},"RightTop":{"X":599,"Y":291}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":4,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"To achieve ultra low power consumption, the chip does not use a conventional, power-consuming restart procedure. The focus of the restart procedure implemented is to ensure a proper supply for the ADC operation only. So it inhibits the ADC until the sensor supply is high enough.","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":480},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":347},"RightBottom":{"X":1651,"Y":480},"RightTop":{"X":1651,"Y":347}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":5,"Type":"title","Text":"##  Table 5 Operating Range","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":564},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":518},"RightBottom":{"X":579,"Y":564},"RightTop":{"X":579,"Y":518}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":6,"Type":"table","Text":"<table><tr><td>Parameter</td><td>Symbol</td><td>min</td><td>typ</td><td>max</td><td>Unit</td><td>Note/Condition</td></tr><tr><td>Operating temperature</td><td>$T_{j}$</td><td>-40</td><td>-</td><td>105</td><td>°C</td><td>$ T_j=T_a+3\\text{ K in fast mode} $</td></tr><tr><td>Supply voltage</td><td>$V_{DD}$</td><td>2.8</td><td>3.3</td><td>3.5</td><td>V</td><td>Supply voltage must be above restart level</td></tr><tr><td>ADC restart level</td><td>$V_{res}$</td><td>2.2</td><td>2.5</td><td>2.8</td><td>V</td><td>min. ADC operating level</td></tr><tr><td>ADC restart hysteresis</td><td>$V_{res-hys}$</td><td>-</td><td>50</td><td>-</td><td>mV</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Register stable level</td><td>$V_{reg}$</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>2.5</td><td>V</td><td>Register values are stable above this voltage level</td></tr></table>","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":973},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":559},"RightBottom":{"X":1645,"Y":973},"RightTop":{"X":1645,"Y":559}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":7,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"The sensor relies on a proper supply ramp defined with $t_{PUP}$, $V_{OUS}$ and $I_{DD-PUP}$, see Figure 6. The I$^{2}$C reset feature of the sensor shall be used by the μC after Power Up. If supply monitoring is used in the system (e.g. brown-out detector etc.), it is also recommended to use the I$^{2}$C reset of the sensor following events detected by this monitor.","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":143,"Y":1168},"LeftTop":{"X":143,"Y":996},"RightBottom":{"X":1645,"Y":1168},"RightTop":{"X":1645,"Y":996}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":8,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"In any case, an external supply switch (either provided by a System-Basis-Chip solution which includes a supply-enable feature, a Bias-Resistor-Transistor device, a capable μC GPIO pin, etc.) shall allow a power-cycle of the sensor as backup for high availability applications to cope with any form of $V_{DD}$ ramps (including potential EMC influences), see Figure 6.","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":1339},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":1178},"RightBottom":{"X":1645,"Y":1339},"RightTop":{"X":1645,"Y":1178}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":9,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"At Power Up, SDA and SCL shall be pulled to $V_{DD}$ using R1 and R2 of Figure 5 and not be driven to low by any device or μC on SDA and SCL.","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":1428},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":1349},"RightBottom":{"X":1649,"Y":1428},"RightTop":{"X":1649,"Y":1349}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":10,"Type":"figure","Text":"","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":290,"Y":1988},"LeftTop":{"X":290,"Y":1458},"RightBottom":{"X":1645,"Y":1988},"RightTop":{"X":1645,"Y":1458}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":[{"Index":0,"Type":"figure_text","Text":"","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":290,"Y":1988},"LeftTop":{"X":290,"Y":1458},"RightBottom":{"X":1645,"Y":1988},"RightTop":{"X":1645,"Y":1458}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":0,"group_type":""}],"ImagePath":"images/be36b61ca518bd04c0e0a68b54092493-image.png","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":11,"Type":"paragraph","Text":"Figure 6 $V_{DD}$ power up and power-cycle for high availability","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":2039},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":1996},"RightBottom":{"X":1031,"Y":2039},"RightTop":{"X":1031,"Y":1996}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id":-1,"group_type":""},{"Index":12,"Type":"footer","Text":"Data Sheet","Level":0,"Polygon":{"LeftBottom":{"X":149,"Y":2451},"LeftTop":{"X":149,"Y":2420},"RightBottom":{"X":288,"Y":2451},"RightTop":{"X":288,"Y":2420}},"InsetImageName":"","Elements":null,"ImagePath":"","group_id